# KNC rsync socket activation

These units run KNC as an inetd-style wait service on the rsync port.  They
expect an executable `/usr/local/libexec/rsync-service` and an rsync daemon
configuration selected by that helper.

Install both units in `/etc/systemd/system`, then run:

```
systemctl daemon-reload
systemctl enable --now knc-rsync.socket
```

The service deliberately retains the capabilities commonly needed by a root
rsync daemon to change ownership, switch users, preserve file metadata and
use a module chroot.  Remove capabilities and add `ReadWritePaths=` entries
when the deployed rsync modules permit tighter restrictions.
